---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CalloutList from "../../components/CalloutList.astro";
import CalloutItem from "../../components/CalloutItem.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playground / CalloutList">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-[900px] px-6 py-16 flex flex-col gap-12">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <a
        href="/playground"
        class="type-label inline-flex items-center gap-1 w-fit"
        style="color: var(--color-text-muted);"
      >
        ← BACK
      </a>
      <p class="type-label" style="color: var(--color-text-eyebrow);">
        COMPONENT
      </p>
      <h1 class="type-display" style="color: var(--color-text-heading);">
        CalloutList
      </h1>
      <p class="type-body" style="color: var(--color-text-body-secondary);">
        List of items with icon chip, title and paragraph. Divider between rows, hidden on the last one.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 class="type-label" style="color: var(--color-text-eyebrow);">
        WARNING VARIANT (2 ITEMS)
      </h2>
      <CalloutList>
        <CalloutItem title="Hours lost answering questions" variant="warning">
          <svg
            slot="icon"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
            <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline>
          </svg>
          In the last year, our team spent up to a day for each question to
          recover the info on changes trough slack, email, and asking around.
        </CalloutItem>
        <CalloutItem
          title="Risk of using wrong components"
          variant="warning"
          iconStyle="outlined"
        >
          <svg
            slot="icon"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path
              d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"
            ></path>
            <line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"></line>
            <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"></line>
          </svg>
          Designers struggled to pick the right version for each project,
          risking outdated components in their flows, and having to replace
          them later.
        </CalloutItem>
      </CalloutList>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 class="type-label" style="color: var(--color-text-eyebrow);">
        INFO VARIANT (3 ITEMS)
      </h2>
      <CalloutList>
        <CalloutItem title="Retrievable" variant="info">
          <svg
            slot="icon"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
            <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
          </svg>
          Changes need to live somewhere stable and be easy to find later.
        </CalloutItem>
        <CalloutItem title="Frictionless" variant="info" iconStyle="outlined">
          <svg
            slot="icon"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M13 2 L3 14 h9 l-1 8 10-12 h-9 z"></path>
          </svg>
          The solution needs to fit into UX/UI workflow as they will be using
          it in their UI Kits.
        </CalloutItem>
        <CalloutItem title="Proactive" variant="info">
          <svg
            slot="icon"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="M18 8A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 7-3 9-3 9h18s-3-2-3-9"></path>
            <path d="M13.73 21a2 2 0 0 1-3.46 0"></path>
          </svg>
          Changes need to reach people, not just wait to be found.
        </CalloutItem>
      </CalloutList>
    </section>

    <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 class="type-label" style="color: var(--color-text-eyebrow);">
        NEUTRAL VARIANT (SINGLE ITEM)
      </h2>
      <CalloutList>
        <CalloutItem title="Single item, no divider" variant="neutral">
          <svg
            slot="icon"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline>
          </svg>
          Any SVG can be passed via <code>slot="icon"</code>. Description text uses
          <code>.type-body</code> (DM Sans Light 16/28).
        </CalloutItem>
      </CalloutList>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
